From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] Drop cpython-freethreading from the cibuildwheel enable
 groups

cibuildwheel 3.0 removed the cpython-freethreading enable group -
free-threaded builds are selected by the build identifier itself now,
not an opt-in group - and its config parser rejects the value outright,
before any container starts and for every interpreter in the matrix:

  Failed to parse enable group. Unknown enable group:
  cpython-freethreading. Valid group names are: cpython-prerelease,
  graalpy, pypy, pypy-eol, pyodide-eol, pyodide-prerelease

Upstream's own dev dependency group pins cibuildwheel>=2.23.3, where
the group is still valid and is what enables its cp313t wheels, so
dropping it upstream would lose those wheels there. Setting
CIBW_ENABLE="" in the workflow env does not help: cibuildwheel merges
the env var's groups into pyproject.toml's list rather than replacing
it, so an empty override leaves cpython-freethreading in place.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [needed only for cibuildwheel 3.0+, which python-wheels pins repo-wide; upstream pins cibuildwheel>=2.23.3]
---
 pyproject.toml | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/pyproject.toml b/pyproject.toml
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/pyproject.toml
+++ b/pyproject.toml
@@ -52,6 +52,5 @@ dev = [
 ]

 [tool.cibuildwheel]
-enable = ["cpython-freethreading"]
 skip = ["*-win32", "cp313t-*"]
 test-groups = ["dev"]
--
2.43.0
